<title>UK: Chelsea up as report raises bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Chelsea up as report raises bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Chelsea Village Plc rose on Monday after a weekend press report said a number of international interests were looking at the company, owner of UK premier league soccer club Chelsea, traders said.</p>
<p>Chelsea shares were up 18p at 115-1/2 by 1043 GMT, though no volume was recorded in the stock.  </p>
<p>A report in the Sunday Telegraph listed George Soros and Granada Group Plc among groups believed to be looking at Chelsea. No-one at the company was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
